{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":312,"name":"Federico Pianzola","username":"fpianz","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.igelsociety.org/fpianz/{size}/188_2.png","created_at":"2022-07-11T07:43:43.416Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://discourse.igelsociety.org/images/emoji/twitter/speech_balloon.png?v=12\" title=\":speech_balloon:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":speech_balloon:\"\u003e \u003cstrong\u003eSpeaker\u003c/strong\u003e: Meghan Sanders\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://discourse.igelsociety.org/images/emoji/twitter/classical_building.png?v=12\" title=\":classical_building:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":classical_building:\"\u003e \u003cstrong\u003eAffiliation\u003c/strong\u003e: Louisiana State University, USA\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTitle\u003c/strong\u003e: \u003cem\u003eBuilding a Better and Just World Through Fictional Narratives\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAbstract\u003c/strong\u003e Scholarship in media psychology has significantly expanded to investigate the role entertainment media and experiences play in encouraging audiences to think more deeply, feel inspired, encourage prosocialness, and otherwise serve in the interest of social good. Fictional narratives are a significant cultural force in that they can articulate identities and values of a culture, but also serve as sites where these same values and identities are discussed and challenged. They can sometimes do a better job than news in getting us to think about the most pressing and serious issues facing communities, nations, and broader society. In this keynote, Sanders will discuss various theoretical frameworks that could help advance our understanding of the psychological mechanisms related to the effects of narratives focused on social justice and those that encourage increased social consciousness.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e**\u003cimg src=\"https://discourse.igelsociety.org/images/emoji/twitter/movie_camera.png?v=12\" title=\":movie_camera:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":movie_camera:\"\u003e**\u003ca href=\"https://youtu.be/m2ZJbIaJ6Q0\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eMeghan Sanders; Building a Better and Just World Through Fictional Narratives - YouTube\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"updated_at":"2022-08-03T18:30:07.615Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":5,"reads":27,"readers_count":26,"score":75.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":248,"topic_slug":"building-a-better-and-just-world-through-fictional-narratives","display_username":"Federico Pianzola","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"version":3,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://youtu.be/m2ZJbIaJ6Q0","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Meghan Sanders; Building a Better and Just World Through Fictional Narratives - YouTube","clicks":3},{"url":"https://discourse.igelsociety.org/t/igel2022-conference-schedule/178","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"IGEL2022 conference schedule","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":1,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"event":null,"calendar_details":[],"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"can_vote":false},{"id":470,"name":"Meghan Sanders","username":"msand","avatar_template":"/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/ccd318/{size}.png","created_at":"2022-07-16T15:23:23.097Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHere is the psychological reactance measure that I referenced:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDillard, J. P., \u0026amp; Shen, L. (2005). On the nature of reactance and its role in persuasive health communication. Communication Monographs, 72, 144-168.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHow much do you agree with each of the following statements?\u003cbr\u003e\n(1 = Strongly Disgree – 5 = Strongly Agree)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eI felt like the general message in the video tried to make a decision for me.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe video tried to manipulate me.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe message in the video tried to pressure me.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe message in the video threatened my freedom to choose what I think.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"updated_at":"2022-07-16T15:23:23.097Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":11,"readers_count":10,"score":47.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":248,"topic_slug":"building-a-better-and-just-world-through-fictional-narratives","display_username":"Meghan Sanders","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":102,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"event":null,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false},{"id":473,"name":"Pamela Pelaez","username":"Pam_Pelaez","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.igelsociety.org/pam_pelaez/{size}/42_2.png","created_at":"2022-07-16T16:22:00.975Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThe media being a tool to socially impact positively and negatively. I am intrigued on how we can measure the effect of having these new narratives about the villains perspective point of view in the viewer and whether we can measure their change in attitude?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLike t